---
import LegalLayout from '~/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '~/config/site';

export const prerender = true;
---

<LegalLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy — ${site.name}`}
  description="What Khoobsurati collects (very little), what it doesn't, and how the shared 'online now' counter and analytics work."
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: August 10, 2026</p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Khoobsurati (<strong>{site.domain}</strong>) is an independent, one-person
    hobby project — a 90s Bollywood internet radio built to feel like a
    neighbourhood ladies' parlour. It isn't a company. Questions about this
    policy can go to <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What Khoobsurati does</h2>
  <p>
    The site plays a curated, looping playlist of 90s Bollywood songs in your
    browser, and links out to the same playlist on Spotify and YouTube Music.
    No account or sign-up exists or is ever required.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>What we don't collect</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>No accounts, no passwords, no user profiles</li>
    <li>No payment information — nothing is for sale</li>
    <li>No contact lists, address books, or precise location</li>
    <li>No forms that collect personal data (the Contact page is a plain email link, not a form)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>The "online now" counter</h3>
  <p>
    While the page is open, your browser generates a random, disposable
    session ID — not tied to your identity in any way — and pings our
    server every few seconds so the page can show roughly how many people
    are listening right now. That ID lives in a small database
    (<a href="https://upstash.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Upstash Redis</a>)
    for at most about two minutes and then expires automatically. It's never
    linked to who you are, never used for anything beyond the live count, and
    isn't shared with anyone.
  </p>

  <h3>Analytics</h3>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics (GA4) to understand, in aggregate, how many
    people visit and roughly where from. It collects page views, approximate
    location (city/region level, derived from IP address), device and
    browser type, and the site that referred you — never your name, email,
    or anything that identifies you individually.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How we use this information</h2>
  <p>
    Solely to (a) keep the shared "listening room" counter running, and (b)
    understand, in aggregate, whether the station is worth keeping running.
    We don't sell data, run ads, or share anything with data brokers —
    there's nothing to sell in the first place.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Cookies</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Cookie</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
          <th>Duration</th>
          <th>Opt out</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code></td>
          <td>Google Analytics — aggregate usage measurement</td>
          <td>Up to 2 years</td>
          <td>
            <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GA opt-out add-on</a>
            or block third-party cookies in your browser
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    No advertising or cross-site tracking cookies are used. We don't
    currently respond to browser "Do Not Track" signals, since the only
    tracking on the site is the aggregate analytics above.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Third-party processors</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Provider</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
          <th>Policy</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Cloudflare</td>
          <td>Hosting, edge delivery, security</td>
          <td><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Upstash</td>
          <td>Redis database for the "online now" counter</td>
          <td><a href="https://upstash.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">upstash.com/privacy</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Google Analytics</td>
          <td>Aggregate usage analytics</td>
          <td><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>YouTube</td>
          <td>In-page audio playback (embedded player)</td>
          <td><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Spotify</td>
          <td>External playlist link (opens on spotify.com)</td>
          <td><a href="https://www.spotify.com/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">spotify.com/legal/privacy-policy</a></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>"Online now" session IDs</strong> — auto-expire after roughly two minutes of inactivity; not kept beyond that</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics data</strong> — retained per Google Analytics' standard aggregate-data window</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs</strong> — we don't keep our own; Cloudflare's standard operational logs apply per their policy above</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because Khoobsurati doesn't hold a personal profile tied to you, there is
    usually nothing on file to access, correct, or delete beyond your
    analytics footprint. If you're in the EEA/UK, you have rights under GDPR
    (access, erasure, objection, and more); if you're in California, you have
    rights under the CCPA (know, delete, opt out of sale — and to be clear,
    <strong>we do not sell personal information</strong>). To exercise any of
    these, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>
    and we'll respond within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>9. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    The site runs on Cloudflare's global edge network, so requests may be
    processed in different countries as part of normal internet routing.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Khoobsurati isn't directed at children under 13, and we don't knowingly
    collect information from them.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served over HTTPS with strict security headers (a locked-down
    Content-Security-Policy, HSTS, and related protections). Since there are
    no accounts, there are no passwords or credentials to leak.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes materially, we'll update it here with a new "Last
    updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy or your data:
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
